Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: reject assignments to WHNAT counters

WHNAT exposes read-only atomic counters through custom module parameter
operations with only a get callback. The permissions prevent sysfs writes,
but a value supplied during parameter parsing still calls the missing
set callback.

Reject assignments with -EPERM while keeping counter reads, arguments and
permissions unchanged. This applies to the local WHNAT extension and does
not change packet forwarding or the writable whnat_enable parameter.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_whnat.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_whnat.c
@@ -52,7 +52,13 @@
 	return sysfs_emit(buf, "%u\n", (unsigned int)atomic_read(kp->arg));
 }
 
+static int counter_set(const char *val, const struct kernel_param *kp)
+{
+	return -EPERM;
+}
+
 static const struct kernel_param_ops counter_ops = {
+	.set = counter_set,
 	.get = counter_get,
 };
 
